WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.733
Matthew, Chapter Seven.

2
00:00:01.733 --> 00:00:04.133
Judge not, that ye be not judged.

3
00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:10.667
For with what judgment ye judge, ye shall be judged: and with what measure ye mete, it shall be measured to you again.

4
00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:17.067
And why beholdest thou the mote that is in thy brother's eye, but considerest not the beam that is in thine own eye?

5
00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:25.333
Or how wilt thou say to thy brother, Let me pull out the mote out of thine eye; and, behold, a beam is in thine own eye?

6
00:00:25.333 --> 00:00:33.333
Thou hypocrite, first cast out the beam out of thine own eye; and then shalt thou see clearly to cast out the mote out of thy brother's eye.

7
00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:43.333
Give not that which is holy unto the dogs, neither cast ye your pearls before swine, lest they trample them under their feet, and turn again and rend you.

8
00:00:43.333 --> 00:00:55.067
Ask, and it shall be given you; seek, and ye shall find; knock, and it shall be opened unto you: For every one that asketh receiveth; and he that seeketh findeth; and to him that knocketh it shall be opened.

9
00:00:55.067 --> 00:01:00.533
Or what man is there of you, whom if his son ask bread, will he give him a stone?

10
00:01:00.533 --> 00:01:02.933
Or if he ask a fish, will he give him a serpent?

11
00:01:02.933 --> 00:01:12.533
If ye then, being evil, know how to give good gifts unto your children, how much more shall your Father which is in heaven give good things to them that ask him?

12
00:01:12.533 --> 00:01:20.667
Therefore all things whatsoever ye would that men should do to you, do ye even so to them: for this is the law and the prophets.

13
00:01:20.667 --> 00:01:35.333
Enter ye in at the strait gate: for wide is the gate, and broad is the way, that leadeth to destruction, and many there be which go in thereat: Because strait is the gate, and narrow is the way, which leadeth unto life, and few there be that find it.

14
00:01:35.333 --> 00:01:40.933
Beware of false prophets, which come to you in sheep's clothing, but inwardly they are ravening wolves.

15
00:01:40.933 --> 00:01:43.733
Ye shall know them by their fruits.

16
00:01:43.733 --> 00:01:47.467
Do men gather grapes of thorns, or figs of thistles?

17
00:01:47.467 --> 00:01:53.467
Even so every good tree bringeth forth good fruit; but a corrupt tree bringeth forth evil fruit.

18
00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:59.333
A good tree cannot bring forth evil fruit, neither can a corrupt tree bring forth good fruit.

19
00:01:59.333 --> 00:02:04.667
Every tree that bringeth not forth good fruit is hewn down, and cast into the fire.

20
00:02:04.667 --> 00:02:07.467
Wherefore by their fruits ye shall know them.

21
00:02:07.467 --> 00:02:16.000
Not every one that saith unto me, Lord, Lord, shall enter into the kingdom of heaven; but he that doeth the will of my Father which is in heaven.

22
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:22.133
Many will say to me in that day, Lord, Lord, have we not prophesied in thy name?

23
00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:24.933
and in thy name have cast out devils?

24
00:02:24.933 --> 00:02:27.333
and in thy name done many wonderful works?

25
00:02:27.333 --> 00:02:33.600
And then will I profess unto them, I never knew you: depart from me, ye that work iniquity.

26
00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:50.133
Therefore whosoever heareth these sayings of mine, and doeth them, I will liken him unto a wise man, which built his house upon a rock: And the rain descended, and the floods came, and the winds blew, and beat upon that house; and it fell not: for it was founded upon a rock.

27
00:02:50.133 --> 00:03:06.667
And every one that heareth these sayings of mine, and doeth them not, shall be likened unto a foolish man, which built his house upon the sand: And the rain descended, and the floods came, and the winds blew, and beat upon that house; and it fell: and great was the fall of it.

28
00:03:06.667 --> 00:03:16.133
And it came to pass, when Jesus had ended these sayings, the people were astonished at his doctrine: For he taught them as one having authority, and not as the scribes.

